{{- /* Facts about this machine that a script cannot work out for itself,
       written by chezmoi on every apply. Sourced by the scripts in
       ~/.local/bin; never a secret, so it is an ordinary 0644 file.

       It exists because the profile set is a template construct while the
       scripts that need it are plain files — `mise run secrets-check` runs one
       straight out of the source tree, so turning them into templates to
       interpolate a vault name would break how they are run and tested.

       Every consumer defaults to the personal vault when this file is missing
       or says nothing, and that is not defensive programming: the secret
       restore runs from the same apply that writes this file, so a
       mid-bootstrap machine genuinely has no copy yet. */ -}}
# Written by chezmoi. No secret material here — see
# docs/design-notes.md, "Profiles".
DOTFILES_PROFILES="{{ includeTemplate "profiles" . }}"
DOTFILES_VAULT="{{ includeTemplate "vault-name" . }}"
